PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Core question requirements: 2019 Toronto Blue Jays player with highest bWAR who:
  1) Played in Game 1 (March 28, 2019 vs. DET);
  2) Played in Game 162 (September 29, 2019 vs. TB);
  3) Placed on the Injured List at least once in 2019 by Toronto.

- Colleague proposals and critiques:
  - Colleague 1 proposed Lourdes Gurriel Jr. (1.8 bWAR).
    - Factual error: Gurriel did NOT play in Game 162. His last game was August 8 before going on the IL with a quad strain, followed by an appendectomy in September.
  - Colleague 2 proposed Teoscar Hernández (1.6 bWAR).
    - Factual error: Hernández was never placed on the Injured List in 2019. His mid-May to early-June absence was an option to Triple-A Buffalo due to performance struggles.
  - Colleague 3 proposed Justin Smoak (0.2 bWAR).
    - Colleague 3 accurately verified all three conditions for Smoak:
      1) Started at 1B on Opening Day (Game 1);
      2) Started at 1B in Game 162 (received a standing ovation in his final game as a Blue Jay);
      3) Placed on 10-day IL on June 15, 2019 (left hamstring/quad strain), activated June 28.
    - Also thoroughly eliminated other candidates who played both games (Grichuk, Hernández, Drury, Tellez - none were on the IL; Gurriel/Giles did not play Game 162).

- Conclusion: Justin Smoak appears to be the only eligible player meeting all three criteria (or at least the highest WAR among the very small subset that actually qualifies). Colleague 3's argument is decisively correct.
}

